Bayar's Comic, Issue 1         NannyMUD Times                        Page 12

    Once upon a time, there was an average guy called Bayar, he had no other
    business except surfing the web. One particular day, while he was
    searching for some guy that eats mud, came across a thing called
    NannyMUD. He clicked the link... and suddenly... all things around him
    started spinning all over the place and fading into oblivion, his desktop
    turning into a void sucking him in.

  Bayar: "What the hell just happened? Where am I? How come I can't see my
          hands? Or my body? Or even feel it? Am I dead?"

  Voice: "I think the most important question is 'What's your name?'
          The other answers come eventually after..."

  Bayar: "Well, this is some weird sh.. uh, my name... my name is Bayar.
          Wait, who and where are you? I demand some answers!"

  Voice: "Calm down. I'm the God of this world. I'm here to guide you. Seems
          you are not from this world..."

  Bayar: "That is corect, I'm not! The next question for the contestant is,
          How do I go back?"

  Mats:  "I'm afraid that this is no simple question. Ok, let me explain.
          You are now in the Void, and I'm working on getting you out.
          But I'm afraid that you will be stuck in this world for a while."

  Bayar: "Ok. Now, this world, what is it called?"

  Mats:  "It is called NannyMUD."

  Bayar: "Oh, just like that link..."

  Mats:  "Link?"

  Bayar: "Never mind that. Tell me something about you and why do you want
          to help me?"

  Mats:  "Well, I'm the God of NannyMUD, I'm perspicacious, and all mortals
          are afraid of my wrath. I want to help you because I'm a nice guy,
          and because you are not from this world."

  Bayar: "Well...fine with me."

  Mats:  "But enough formalities. Tell me, are you male, female or other?"

  Bayar: "Male, last I checked."

  Mats:  "Everything seems to be in order, we will arrive to the village
          church shortly. You will have to seek guidance there. I should not
          interfere with mortals, but since you are a special case, I'll make
          an exception. Just don't call me, I'll call you."

  Bayar: "Got it."

  Mats:  "Well, this is where I get off. Be careful, and good luck!"

  Bayar: "Thanks."

  Bayar to himself:
    "Seems like this was a good example of divine intervention."

  Announcement: "We will arrive to the village church in 2 minutes.
                 Please take your personal belongings and prepare to leave."


(The voice of Mats used in this comic is fictional.)

